+ * Durable run root for resumable children (`agents.childSession`).
+ *
+ * A managed temporary run root lives under the OS temp directory (`tmpfs` on
+ * Linux) and is removed when its session closes, so a child that outlived a
+ * host crash, a reboot, or a session restart lost the transcript and the
+ * `resume.json` launch authority that `agents.resume` re-executes. The runs of a
+ * resumable session therefore live under the user cache directory, keyed by the
+ * Pi session id they belong to: continuing that same session (`pi -c`, after a
+ * reboot too) finds the same root and its settled runs again, while another
+ * session never adopts them.
